
# 2026-03-20 08:56:49.082977
+BUG DESCRIPTION --------------- Actual Behavior: GET /items/{id} raises a KeyError and causes a 500 crash when the item does not exist. GET /items/{id}/total raises a ZeroDivisionError when the item's quantity is 0, causing a 500 crash. DELETE /items/{id} can raise a KeyError for missing items and currently returns an empty/no body response on successful deletion with no proper status code. Expected Behavior: GET /items/{id} should return HTTP 404 with a JSON error when the item does not exist instead of crashing. GET /items/{id}/total should validate quantity and return HTTP 400 with a descriptive error when quantity is 0, avoiding exceptions. DELETE /items/{id} should return HTTP 204 No Content on successful deletion and HTTP 404 with a JSON error when the item does not exist. No unhandled exceptions should be raised by these endpoints. Affected Area: Items API endpoints: GET /items/{id}, GET /items/{id}/total, DELETE /items/{id} ASSUMPTIONS ----------- - ⚠️ The implementation accesses item dictionary keys or database rows without existence checks, causing KeyError on missing items. - ⚠️ The total calculation performs a division by quantity without validating non-zero, causing ZeroDivisionError. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA ------------------- 1. Given a non-existent item id, when GET /items/{id} is called, then respond with HTTP 404 and JSON body {'error': 'item not found'} and do not throw any server exception. 2. Given an item with quantity 0, when GET /items/{id}/total is called, then respond with HTTP 400 and JSON body {'error': 'invalid quantity'} and do not throw any exception. 3. No regression in items endpoints; specifically, when DELETE /items/{id} is called for an existing item respond with HTTP 204 No Content, and when called for a non-existent item respond with HTTP 404 and JSON body {'error': 'item not found'}.
+
+  Instructions:
+  - Read the repo map and find the relevant files yourself.
+  - Make the minimal, targeted change needed.
+  - Do not refactor unrelated code.
+  - Do not create new files unless necessary.
+  

